          "id": "S001",
          "text": "Fix a smooth real mean-zero datum u0 and assume L1: ||u0||_(H^gamma)<=R. H001-H003 and N001 give a common M bound depending only on T,gamma,R. Take the exact u from N001, put v=S_(-t)u, construct V by Interp, and set e=v-V. N001 identifies u as a smooth solution of u_t+u_xxx=u*u_x=(1/2)*partial_x(u^2) and v=S_(-t)u, so the explicit normalized exact-solution premise of N010 is satisfied. Use N010 with a constant C_M enlarged to work throughout this ball. Define N=ceil(max(2,8*C_M,(8*C_M)^(14/23))). Then C_M(N^(-1)+N^(-23/14))<=1/4. Then choose delta in (0,1] so small that C_M delta(N^2+3)<=1/4, and restrict tau<=delta/2. On any interval starting at a grid point and of length h<=delta with error supremum <=1, N010 absorbs the error coefficient: h+tau<=3delta/2, and hence E_I<=2||e(a)||_2+C'_M delta*tau^gamma. These choices depend only on the common M and gamma,T.",
