          "text": "Partition the grid into blocks of floor(delta/tau) steps and a possibly shorter final block. Full block lengths belong to [delta/2,delta], so there are at most 2T/delta+1 blocks. Iterate F001, beginning with e(0)=0, to get sup_[0,t]||e||_2<=K*tau^gamma on every prefix on which ||e||_2<=1; K depends only on T,gamma,R. This includes a prefix ending inside the last step, because N010 explicitly allows a partial final interval. N007 gives continuity of the interpolant; the exact solution is continuous by N001. For contradiction assume L2: the error first reaches one at a time in [0,T]. At that first time, the same finite recurrence through that first time would give <=K*tau^gamma. Choose tau0<=min(1,delta/2) so small that K*tau0^gamma<1/2, possible because H002 gives gamma>0. This contradicts L2, which is discharged; hence the estimate holds on all [0,T]. N007 gives V(t_n)=S_(-t_n)u^n and N001 gives unitarity of the twist, so the grid-point bound follows. No bound depends on higher smooth norms or spectral support. Discharge L1 into the datum-ball antecedent and quantify over all such smooth data.",
